Package: trackpad-like-mac
Version: @VERSION@
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Architecture: @ARCH@
Installed-Size: @SIZE@
Depends: python3 (>= 3.9), systemd
Recommends: gnome-shell (>= 45), python3-gi
Maintainer: Burak Beyler <burakbeyler@icloud.com>
Homepage: https://github.com/beylerburak/trackpad-like-mac
Description: macOS-style touchpad gestures for Linux
 Makes a Linux touchpad behave like a MacBook trackpad: three-finger drag,
 four-finger swipes for workspaces and the overview, thumb-and-three-finger
 pinches for the app grid and desktop, a right-edge swipe for notifications
 and scrolling that follows the fingers. Gestures beyond dragging need
 GNOME Shell 45 or later.
